{"kind":"assert","text":"Question for the cutover head (05d618e2). Replay cannot check an entry that uses a private sequence's genesis fact. The fix changes production replay code. WIP head 10ffa822.\n\nThe case: a Directory entry (seq 2) uses the Membership genesis fact {at, seq 0, hash = at.genesis} under pin platform:membership@8, and its copy is the 4,550-byte Membership genesis entry. Under 5a642337 and 066e49b3, replay must prove a Membership fact by an anchor, so the test anchors it.\n- The cutover's verify.ts anchoredCopy refuses any copy whose input is genesis (verify.ts:107). Replay stops with \"the anchored source lacks an exact canonical raw copy\".\n- Without the anchor, #prove has no Membership history and stops with missing-dependency.\n- Main had no such refusal, because the cutover added anchoredCopy.\n- The #birth path under ae48dd39 skips seq-0 uses, so nothing admits a used foreign genesis.\n- So at this head, replay of any Directory that reads a Membership genesis fails. The two driver resume tests show it.\n\nChoose one:\n(a) Replay admits a used foreign genesis with no anchor, by admitSequenceGenesis(bytes, fact.at), because a genesis's hash is its at.genesis. The kind comes from the checked sequence and must equal the recorded kind, which is the same check as #birth. This proves the fact from the copied body. 5a642337 point 2 says replay proves no register or membership fact from a copied body, so (a) changes that contract. For this one case it is stronger than an anchor, because the bytes prove themselves.\n(b) anchoredCopy accepts a genesis copy when fact.seq is 0 and fact.hash equals fact.at.genesis, and it still requires the anchor. This stays within 5a642337 and 066e49b3. The report lists the genesis as taken on the caller's word, as it lists any other anchored fact.\n\nI recommend (b) for this head. It keeps the anchor contract unchanged, and it only removes a refusal that the cutover added and main lacked. (a) is a sound later improvement, and it belongs in its own review, because it narrows the caller's-word list that 5a642337 defines.\n\nMeanwhile the lane fixes archive-installed (9) and device-install."}